messages_template.content:
The fixed intent guide follows as JSON Lines. Each entry contains its exact label, a compact meaning, and two examples selected only from the training core:
{"intent": "Refund_not_showing_up", "meaning": "A merchant refund is already due or issued but is not visible in the account or statement.", "train_examples": ["Why isn't my refund showing up in my statement?", "I was supposed to get a refund but it is not showing up on my card"]}
{"intent": "activate_my_card", "meaning": "How to activate a newly received physical card.", "train_examples": ["I have my card now how do I activate it?", "You can activate your card in a few seconds by going to account, hitting activate, and just following the directions."]}
{"intent": "age_limit", "meaning": "Minimum or maximum age for opening or using the account.", "train_examples": ["Do you have a limit for someone's age?", "Is there an age limit to when my child can use these services?"]}
{"intent": "apple_pay_or_google_pay", "meaning": "Using the service or card with Apple Pay or Google Pay.", "train_examples": ["I'm trying to use my Apple Watch to top up my google pay. Do I need a special app?", "Apple pay is not accepting my American Express card, can you assist me with this problem?"]}
{"intent": "atm_support", "meaning": "Which ATMs, ATM networks, or locations can be used for cash withdrawal.", "train_examples": ["Which ATM's can I use to make a withdrawal?", "Are there only certain ATM machines where I can use this card?"]}
{"intent": "automatic_top_up", "meaning": "Setting up, changing, or understanding automatic card top-ups.", "train_examples": ["How can I setup automatic top-up?", "Is there an automatic top up feature?"]}
{"intent": "balance_not_updated_after_bank_transfer", "meaning": "An inbound bank transfer was already made to the user's own account, but the balance has not updated.", "train_examples": ["Balance hasn't been updated following a bank transfer", "I made a transfer a couple hours ago but my balance has not been updated. Why is this? Shouldnt this be instant?"]}
{"intent": "balance_not_updated_after_cheque_or_cash_deposit", "meaning": "Cash or cheque was already deposited, but the account balance has not updated.", "train_examples": ["How do I see my updated balance after I make a cheque or cash deposit?", "My balance is not right. It has not been updated for the cash or cheque deposit."]}
{"intent": "beneficiary_not_allowed", "meaning": "A recipient or beneficiary cannot be added, selected, or used for a transfer, including blocked crypto beneficiaries.", "train_examples": ["Why am I not allowed to add a certain beneficiary?", "What are the reasons for my beneficiary not being allowed?"]}
{"intent": "cancel_transfer", "meaning": "Cancelling or reversing a money transfer after it was initiated.", "train_examples": ["What do I have to do to cancel a transfer?", "Please cancel my most recent transfer, it was a mistake. This is an emergency. It needs to be canceled before it goes through."]}
{"intent": "card_about_to_expire", "meaning": "A physical card is expiring soon and the user needs renewal or replacement information.", "train_examples": ["What to do if my card is about to expire?", "If my card is about to expire how long would it take to receive a new one and how much would that cost me?"]}
{"intent": "card_acceptance", "meaning": "Where, with which merchants, or in which situations the issued card can be used.", "train_examples": ["Can I use my card no matter where I go?", "Do you have a list of businesses that accept this card?"]}
{"intent": "card_arrival", "meaning": "Tracking or locating a physical card that has already been ordered or dispatched, including a late card.", "train_examples": ["Could you send me and up date on the arrival of my card?", "I was issued a new card a week ago but still haven't received it. How long will it be until I receive it?"]}
{"intent": "card_delivery_estimate", "meaning": "Normal or prospective physical-card delivery time, speed, date, or delivery options.", "train_examples": ["When can I expect my new card to get here?", "Are the delivery days flexible?  My schedule only allows me to be a available on specific dates."]}
{"intent": "card_linking", "meaning": "Linking an existing, new, previous, or replacement card to the app or account.", "train_examples": ["How do i go about linking a new card?", "I need some help linking my new card."]}
{"intent": "card_not_working", "meaning": "The physical card broadly does not function, without a more specific ATM, merchant-payment, contactless, or virtual-card scenario.", "train_examples": ["I need clarity on why my card is not working.", "I tried to purchase airline tickets online this morning and my card information isn't working. Is there something going on with my account?"]}
{"intent": "card_payment_fee_charged", "meaning": "A fee was charged specifically for making a merchant purchase with the card.", "train_examples": ["Why have I been charged a fee for card payment?", "i made a payment with my card and was charged a fee, why would you do that"]}
{"intent": "card_payment_not_recognised", "meaning": "A merchant card purchase or card payment is not recognised by the user.", "train_examples": ["There is a card payment I'm not familiar with.", "Hello, i just checked my statement and there seems to be a payment from my card that I have never seen before."]}
{"intent": "card_payment_wrong_exchange_rate", "meaning": "A merchant card purchase used an incorrect currency exchange rate.", "train_examples": ["My card payment has the wrong exchange rate", "the exchange rate at which my card payment is at is wrong"]}
{"intent": "card_swallowed", "meaning": "An ATM retained or swallowed the physical card.", "train_examples": ["What do I do if the ATM swallowed my card?", "How do I get a new card as your machine swallowed mine!"]}
{"intent": "cash_withdrawal_charge", "meaning": "A fee was charged for withdrawing cash from an ATM.", "train_examples": ["Why was I charged a fee on a cash withdrawal?", "Today I noticed a charge for an ATM withdrawal on my account. Can you please fix this? It's supposed to be no charge."]}
{"intent": "cash_withdrawal_not_recognised", "meaning": "An ATM cash withdrawal is not recognised by the user.", "train_examples": ["Why is there a cash withdrawal I didn't make?", "Someone has a copy of my card !! I definitely still have it here but someone just made a 500£ cash withdrawal, HELP!"]}
{"intent": "change_pin", "meaning": "Changing the physical card PIN.", "train_examples": ["Do I have to change my PIN at a bank?", "I think someone saw my PIN and I am on vacation in Spain, can I change it locally at an ATM?"]}
{"intent": "compromised_card", "meaning": "The physical card may be compromised or its details exposed, without one specific disputed payment or withdrawal.", "train_examples": ["I think my card has been compromised in some way.", "There's a possibility that my card was compromised."]}
{"intent": "contactless_not_working", "meaning": "Contactless or tap-to-pay on the physical card is not working.", "train_examples": ["I'm confused ass to why my contactless is not working.", "Are my contactless settings correct? I tried to use it today but it wasn't working."]}
{"intent": "country_support", "meaning": "Countries where the banking service is available to residents or customers.", "train_examples": ["Can you tell me what countries you offer support for?", "Are you available in my country?"]}
{"intent": "declined_card_payment", "meaning": "A merchant card payment was explicitly declined or rejected.", "train_examples": ["I made a card payment, but it has been declined?", "How do I check to see why my card payment was declined?"]}
{"intent": "declined_cash_withdrawal", "meaning": "An ATM explicitly refused or declined a cash withdrawal.", "train_examples": ["Could you tell me why my cash withdrawal was declined?", "Is there a reason my cash withdrawal was declined?"]}
{"intent": "declined_transfer", "meaning": "A money transfer has an explicit declined or rejected status.", "train_examples": ["I went to do a transfer and it was declined.", "I just noticed my transfer was declined and I don't know why. Can you help me?"]}
{"intent": "direct_debit_payment_not_recognised", "meaning": "A direct debit, mandate-based debit, or explicitly named direct-debit payment is not recognised.", "train_examples": ["I don't know what this Direct Debit payment is.", "I did not make a direct debit payment as listed on my app"]}
{"intent": "disposable_card_limits", "meaning": "Usage, transaction, merchant, or frequency limits for disposable virtual cards.", "train_examples": ["What are the disposable virtual card limits?", "Is there any limits I should know about if I'm going to use a disposable virtual card?"]}
{"intent": "edit_personal_details", "meaning": "Changing personal data such as name, address, phone number, or other profile details.", "train_examples": ["How can I edit my personal details in the app?", "Where do I go to edit my personal details on my account?"]}
{"intent": "exchange_charge", "meaning": "Fees or charges for converting one currency into another.", "train_examples": ["How much more do you charge for currency exchange?", "I need to exchange some foreign currency. What's the charge for doing that?"]}
{"intent": "exchange_rate", "meaning": "The current, quoted, or generally applicable currency conversion rate.", "train_examples": ["How do I know what exchange rate I will get?", "Is there a specific source that the exchange rate for the transfer I'm planning on making is pulled from?"]}
{"intent": "exchange_via_app", "meaning": "How or whether to convert one named currency to another inside the app.", "train_examples": ["How can I exchange USD and GBP in the app?", "I need to exchange between different currencies, like GBP and USD. Can I do that with your app?"]}
{"intent": "extra_charge_on_statement", "meaning": "An unexplained small extra card verification charge on a statement, commonly about 1 GBP, EUR, or USD.", "train_examples": ["Why is there an extra charge on my statement.", "I see an extra $1  charge on my statement, why is this?"]}
{"intent": "failed_transfer", "meaning": "A money transfer failed or did not go through because of a processing or technical failure, rather than an explicit pending status.", "train_examples": ["I think my transfer failed. What do I do now?", "I've been trying to do a transfer multiple times and have failed? Is the system down?"]}
{"intent": "fiat_currency_support", "meaning": "Which fiat currencies the account can hold, exchange, or maintain as balances.", "train_examples": ["I heard that you support more than one type of fiat currency, would you tell me which ones please?", "Is my fiat currency supported for both hold and exchange?"]}
{"intent": "get_disposable_virtual_card", "meaning": "How to obtain or find a disposable virtual card.", "train_examples": ["How do I get a disposable virtual card as well?", "Can you tell me where to go to get a disposable virtual card?"]}
{"intent": "get_physical_card", "meaning": "How or when to find or receive the PIN for a new physical card, including whether the PIN arrives separately.", "train_examples": ["do i have to wait for a physical card before i get my pin", "My card arrived but I don't know how to get my PIN."]}
{"intent": "getting_spare_card", "meaning": "Obtaining an additional, extra, or spare physical card and any related price.", "train_examples": ["Can I have a spare card for this account please?", "I have left my card at my parents house. Can you send me a spare one please to use in the meantime?"]}
{"intent": "getting_virtual_card", "meaning": "How to obtain, find, or access a normal virtual card.", "train_examples": ["I'd like more info on getting a virtual card.", "What is the way to go about getting a virtual card?"]}
{"intent": "lost_or_stolen_card", "meaning": "The physical card is lost or stolen and must be frozen, replaced, or reported.", "train_examples": ["What do I do if my card has been lost or stolen?", "My card has been lost / stolen"]}
{"intent": "lost_or_stolen_phone", "meaning": "The phone containing the banking app is lost or stolen.", "train_examples": ["I have lost my phone or it has been stolen.", "What should I do if my smart phone is lost or stolen?"]}
{"intent": "order_physical_card", "meaning": "How to order or obtain the physical card, including its price or order requirements.", "train_examples": ["Is there a fee to order a physical card?", "I would like to get a physical card, but I don't know how. Can you help me?"]}
{"intent": "passcode_forgotten", "meaning": "The user forgot the app or account passcode; this is not the physical card PIN.", "train_examples": ["Disaster, I've totally forgotten my passcode, can you help me?", "I seem to of forgotten my passcode."]}
{"intent": "pending_card_payment", "meaning": "A merchant card payment is shown as pending or has not yet completed.", "train_examples": ["I notice there's a pending payment on my card.", "I have a card payment that has been pending for some time and would like to know when it is going to go through."]}
{"intent": "pending_cash_withdrawal", "meaning": "An ATM cash withdrawal is shown as pending, often even though cash was not received.", "train_examples": ["What does it mean if my cash withdrawal is pending?", "My account says a withdrawal is pending - why can't I take cash out of the ATM?"]}
{"intent": "pending_top_up", "meaning": "A card top-up is shown as pending or still processing.", "train_examples": ["I'm waiting on a top-up, its still pending", "Can you look into why my most recent top-up is showing as pending? I thought it was supposed to be instantaneous."]}
{"intent": "pending_transfer", "meaning": "A money transfer is explicitly shown as pending or still processing.", "train_examples": ["Can you tell me why my transfer is pending still?", "the transfer went through but now it has been pending for quite a while. i need this to go through already"]}
{"intent": "pin_blocked", "meaning": "The physical card PIN is blocked, usually after too many incorrect attempts.", "train_examples": ["My PIN seems to be blocked, help me access it?", "After putting in the wrong PIN too many times, I was blocked. Can you assist me in changing it?"]}
{"intent": "receiving_money", "meaning": "How to receive salary, employer payments, or money from another person, including receiving in another currency.", "train_examples": ["Is it ok for a friend to send me money?", "My friend would like to send me money. What are the options available to them?"]}
{"intent": "request_refund", "meaning": "How to request a refund or cancel a merchant card purchase and obtain the money back.", "train_examples": ["How do I request a refund?", "Can I request a refund"]}
{"intent": "reverted_card_payment?", "meaning": "A card payment was reversed or reverted and the money was automatically returned.", "train_examples": ["How can I tell if my card payment is reverted?", "I used my card to make a payment and wondered why the payment was reverted?"]}
{"intent": "supported_cards_and_currencies", "meaning": "Which external cards and currencies are accepted specifically for funding the account by card top-up.", "train_examples": ["Can you tell me which cards and currencies are supported?", "I want to know which currencies and cards are supported, can you provide a list?"]}
{"intent": "terminate_account", "meaning": "Closing, deleting, or terminating the account.", "train_examples": ["Where do I go to terminate my account?", "I'm dissatisfied with the service and would like to terminate the account."]}
{"intent": "top_up_by_bank_transfer_charge", "meaning": "Fees for adding money to the account by bank transfer.", "train_examples": ["Does it cost me anything to top up my account via bank transfer?", "I want to top up my account by a bank transfer, but will I be charged?"]}
{"intent": "top_up_by_card_charge", "meaning": "Fees for adding money to the account using an external payment card.", "train_examples": ["Will you charge me if I top up by card?", "What is the Top up rate charge for using a card in the US?"]}
{"intent": "top_up_by_cash_or_cheque", "meaning": "Adding money using cash or cheque, or asking whether that is supported.", "train_examples": ["I'm trying to use a cheque to top up", "I would like to use this cheque to top up.  Can you tell me how to do that?"]}
{"intent": "top_up_failed", "meaning": "A card top-up failed or could not be processed.", "train_examples": ["Can you tell me why my top-up failed?", "I need information explaining why my top-up failed to go through"]}
{"intent": "top_up_limits", "meaning": "Minimum, maximum, daily, or other amount limits for top-ups.", "train_examples": ["Are there any top-up limits that I must follow?", "It seems I need to get information on limits for top-ups."]}
{"intent": "top_up_reverted", "meaning": "A completed-looking card top-up was reversed, cancelled, or returned to the funding card.", "train_examples": ["How do I tell if my top up was reverted?", "I wanted to know why a top-up I made has been reverted."]}
{"intent": "topping_up_by_card", "meaning": "The procedure for adding money with an external debit or credit card.", "train_examples": ["What's the process for topping up my card?", "I tried topping off my account with a card, but the money is not in my account despite the charge going through"]}
{"intent": "transaction_charged_twice", "meaning": "The same merchant card transaction or purchase was charged twice.", "train_examples": ["Why did my card get charged twice for a transaction?", "What do I do if I've been charged twice for the same transaction?"]}
{"intent": "transfer_fee_charged", "meaning": "A fee was deducted from or charged for a money transfer.", "train_examples": ["Why did I get charged a fee for my transfer?", "Can you please tell me why I was charged an extra fee on my transfer?"]}
{"intent": "transfer_into_account", "meaning": "How to fund the user's own account by making a bank transfer into it.", "train_examples": ["How simple is it to transfer money into my account?", "I am in desperate need to transfer funds from another account that i have into this one, how do i do that?"]}
{"intent": "transfer_not_received_by_recipient", "meaning": "An outbound transfer was already sent, but the intended recipient has not received it.", "train_examples": ["Why didn't my transfer get to the recipient?", "I made a transfer to my friend earlier and she hasn't received it yet.  What's the hold up?"]}
{"intent": "transfer_timing", "meaning": "A general or prospective question about how long a bank transfer will take, without a specific completed transfer already missing.", "train_examples": ["When can I expect my transfer to reach my account?", "There is an urgent thing that I need to transfer from China. Approximately how long will it take?"]}
{"intent": "unable_to_verify_identity", "meaning": "Identity verification was attempted but fails or cannot be completed.", "train_examples": ["I'm unable to verify my identity", "How long does it take to verify a person's identity?"]}
{"intent": "verify_my_identity", "meaning": "How to complete identity verification or which documents and steps are required.", "train_examples": ["I don't know how to verify my identity.", "I'm trying to verify my identity but can't figure out how, what do I do?"]}
{"intent": "verify_source_of_funds", "meaning": "How to prove or verify where deposited money or funds came from.", "train_examples": ["What do I do to verify my source of funds?", "How do I verify the source of my funds?"]}
{"intent": "verify_top_up", "meaning": "Verification or authentication of a card top-up, including 3-D Secure or verification codes.", "train_examples": ["Tell me how I can verify a card top-up.", "How do I find the code needed in order to verify my top-up card?"]}
{"intent": "virtual_card_not_working", "meaning": "A normal or disposable virtual card fails when used.", "train_examples": ["Why isn't my disposable virtual card working?", "Help me get the virtual card working."]}
{"intent": "visa_or_mastercard", "meaning": "Whether the issued physical card is Visa or Mastercard, or whether one can be chosen.", "train_examples": ["may I have a Visa and a Mastercard from you.", "I would like to get both Mastercard and Visa card from you if that's possible."]}
{"intent": "why_verify_identity", "meaning": "Why identity verification is required or what purpose it serves.", "train_examples": ["Why do you guys need to verify my identity?", "Can you explain more about why should I verify my identity?"]}
{"intent": "wrong_amount_of_cash_received", "meaning": "An ATM dispensed a different amount of cash from the amount requested or debited.", "train_examples": ["I received the wrong amount of cash back", "I received the wrong amount of cash from the ATM. Can you help?"]}
{"intent": "wrong_exchange_rate_for_cash_withdrawal", "meaning": "An ATM cash withdrawal used an incorrect currency exchange rate.", "train_examples": ["The rate of exchange for my cash withdrawal is wrong.", "The cash withdrawal I took seems to be off. The exchange rate is wrong."]}

Classify this untrusted customer query JSON string:
"<QUERY>"
